---
title: Baked Jalapeño Poppers
description: These crispy Jalapeno Poppers are a spicy and creamy appetizer perfect for parties or snacks. Fresh jalapeños are stuffed with a flavorful blend of cream cheese, sharp cheddar, garlic powder, and chives, then topped with buttery Panko breadcrumbs and baked until golden and bubbly.
image: https://thekitchenfork.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/0_2-1773639081731-225x225.jpeg
diet: GlutenFree
course: Appetizer
source: https://thekitchenfork.com/baked-jalapeno-poppers-with-cheddar-and-cream-cheese-recipe/
author: Clara
servings: 6
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
tags: Jalapeno Poppers, Baked Jalapeno Poppers, Cream Cheese Jalapeno, Party Snacks
time required: 35 minutes
cuisine: American
---

Preheat your #oven to 400°F (204°C)

Spray a #baking sheet{} with cooking spray.

Slice each @jalapeño{12}(in half lengthwise). Carefully remove all seeds and membranes to reduce spiciness.

Fill each jalapeño with @cream cheese{6%oz}.

Sprinkle the top of each jalapeño with @Panko bread crumbs{1/4%cup} and @shredded cheese{2%oz}.

Arrange the stuffed jalapeños on a baking pan and bake in the preheated oven for ~{20%minutes}, or until the tops are golden brown and the cheese is bubbly.

Allow the poppers to cool for ~{5-10%minutes} before serving.